---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Devices"
  description="Published device integration notes for auroraADE."
  current="devices"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <h1>Devices</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      Published device integration notes for auroraADE. The status below is
      preserved from the previous project status page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="document-section">
    <header class="document-heading">
      <span class="document-index">01</span>
      <h2>Last published status</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="document-body">
      <div class="device-status-list">
        <div class="device-status-row">
          <h3>Desktop</h3>
          <p>Runtime integration pending. The browser runtime was not connected to a desktop build in the last published status.</p>
          <strong class="status-word status-pending">Pending</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="device-status-row">
          <h3>Mobile</h3>
          <p>No mobile build was available in the last published status.</p>
          <strong class="status-word status-unavailable">Unavailable</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="document-section">
    <header class="document-heading">
      <span class="document-index">02</span>
      <h2>Platform target</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="document-body">
      <p>auroraADE's documented target architecture is x86_64. The wider Fabric Dessert CPU integration boundary is designed to accommodate ARM 32-bit, ARM 64-bit, x86 32-bit and x86 64-bit integrations; that broader boundary should not be confused with auroraADE's own target.</p>
      <a class="metro-link" href="/architecture/">Architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
